CrmSequenceIntro=A sequence is the follow-up plan for enrolled deals. The hourly job runs one due step per enrolment, and only while this sequence is active and customer sequences are enabled. With dry-run on, e-mails are recorded in the journal and not sent. In draft mode, an e-mail step becomes a planned e-mail for the salesperson instead of being sent.
CrmStepsHelp=Add the steps in the order they should run. The delay is the number of days after enrolment, not after the previous step. An e-mail goes to the deal contact. A call or a task creates an agenda event on the deal and sends nothing. The table shows position, kind, delay and subject. The body is used only for an e-mail and is not listed here.
CrmEnrolmentsHelp=Pick the open deal to enrol; type to search by reference, title or account. The sequence must already have a step, and the deal must not already be running on it. The table lists each enrolment: the deal, the status (running, stopped or done), the position of the step waiting to run, when that step is due, and why it stopped. Stop ends it yourself. Mark replied ends it because the contact answered; the mailbox is not read. A won or lost deal is stopped on the next run. After the last step, the status becomes done.
CrmJournalHelp=Each row is one e-mail attempt, newest first: when it ran, the contact address, the subject after the placeholders were replaced, and the result (sent, simulated, draft or error). A draft is an e-mail step turned into a planned e-mail on the deal for the salesperson. Calls and tasks are not listed here.
