CrmNewPipelineHelp=A pipeline is a separate sales process with its own stages and probabilities, for example new customers, renewals or partners. The reference is fixed once created (letters, digits, underscore, dash). A new pipeline starts empty unless you copy the stages of another one; it needs at least one open stage, one won stage and one lost stage before deals can be created in it.
CrmEditPipelineHelp=A pipeline that is not active is no longer offered when creating a deal or on the board. Its existing deals stay in the lists and reports. The last active pipeline cannot be deactivated.
CrmPipelineNoOpenStage=This pipeline has no open stage: no deal can be created in it until you add one.
CrmErrorPipelineLabelRequired=A label is required.
CrmErrorPipelineRefRequired=A reference is required (letters, digits, underscore or dash).
CrmErrorPipelineRefExists=A pipeline with this reference already exists.
CrmErrorPipelineNotFound=Pipeline not found.
CrmErrorLastPipeline=The last active pipeline cannot be deactivated.
CrmAiAssistant=AI assistant
CrmAiIntro=Ask %s to read the deal and the e-mails exchanged so far and propose the next e-mail. The deal summary, the exchange and your current text are sent to that service.
CrmAiMasked=Names, addresses and references are masked before sending (AI module privacy setting).
CrmAiNotMasked=They are not masked: do not use this on exchanges that must not leave the company.
CrmAiSuggest=Suggest a reply with AI
CrmAiRestorePrompt=Restore the default prompt
CrmAiHelp=You can edit the prompt for this request. The proposal replaces the text above, but nothing is saved or sent: read it, change it, then use the buttons below. Reload the page to get back the saved draft.
CrmAiInserted=Proposal inserted in the text. Read and edit it before sending: nothing has been saved or sent.
CrmAiError=The AI service did not answer: %s
CrmAiGoToSetup=Check the AI module setup
CrmErrorAiNoDeal=Deal not found.
CrmErrorAiNoAnswer=The AI service returned no answer.
CrmAiEmailAssist=AI assistant in the e-mail editor
CrmAiEmailAssistHelp=Off by default. Set 1 to show the "Suggest a reply with AI" block in the e-mail editor when the AI module is enabled; 0 hides it. When it is on, the text of the deal and of the exchange is sent to the AI service set up in the AI module.
CrmAiEmailPrompt=Default AI prompt
CrmAiEmailPromptHelp=The prompt offered to salespeople, who can edit it for each request. Empty uses the built-in prompt.
CrmAiDefaultPrompt=Read the e-mail exchange below with our prospect and write our next e-mail. Be polite, concise and concrete. Answer every question the prospect asked. Do not invent prices, dates, features or commitments that are not in the exchange or the deal. Propose a clear next step with a date when it fits. Write in the language of the prospect's last message and sign with the salesperson's first name.
CrmAiWaiting=Waiting for the AI service... (this can take half a minute)
CrmFormat=Format
CrmFormatHtml=Formatted (HTML), sent with a plain-text version
CrmFormatText=Plain text only
CrmFormatHelp=HTML lets you format the message (bold, lists, links). It is sent together with a plain-text version made from it, so a mail program that shows no formatting still reads the message. Plain text is sent as it is. Going back to plain text loses the formatting. With your own mail client: "Open in my mail client" fills in the plain-text version, and "Copy text" copies the formatted version, to paste into the message.
CrmTabHtml=Formatted (HTML)
CrmTabPlain=Plain text
CrmTabPlainAlt=Plain-text version (automatic)
CrmPlainAlternativeNote=Made from the formatted message when it is sent: edit the formatted tab. A link address is not repeated here, so write the address in the text when it matters.
CrmConfirmToText=Switch to plain text? The formatting is lost.
CrmConfirmDryRunOff=Switch dry-run off? From now on the sequence job sends real e-mails to customers (in "Send automatically" mode).
CrmConfirmReminderDryRunOff=Switch the reminder dry-run off? From now on the daily digest is really e-mailed to deal owners.
CrmConfirmAiOn=Switch the AI assistant on? The text of deals and e-mail exchanges will be sent to the AI service set up in the AI module.
CrmSwitchHelp=The on/off switches are saved as soon as you click them; the other fields are saved with the Save button.
CrmStepMode=E-mail mode
CrmStepModeDefault=Default (%s)
CrmStepModeDraft=Draft for the salesperson
CrmStepModeSend=Send automatically
CrmStepModeHelp=For an e-mail step only. Draft: the step becomes a planned e-mail that the salesperson reviews and sends. Send automatically: the job sends it (the dry-run setting applies). Default: follows the global setting "Sequence e-mail steps".
CrmSequenceActiveHelp=Active: the job runs its due steps. An inactive sequence waits; its enrolments resume when it is active again.
CrmStopRules=Stop rules
CrmStopOnReply=Stop an enrolment when the contact replies
CrmStopOnWon=Stop an enrolment when the deal is won
CrmStopOnLost=Stop an enrolment when the deal is lost
CrmSequenceUpdateHelp=The reference is the short code shown in lists and must be unique (letters, digits, underscore, dash). Changing anything here does not touch the steps or the enrolments: a running enrolment goes on with the new rules. Steps already due when an inactive sequence is reactivated run at the next job run.
CrmErrorSequenceNotFound=Sequence not found.
CrmErrorSequenceLabelRequired=A label is required.
CrmErrorSequenceRefInvalid=The reference is required: letters, digits, underscore or dash, 32 characters at most.
CrmErrorSequenceRefExists=Another sequence already uses this reference.
